    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "Driven by seasonal climate conditions that increased border pressure, enforcement actions rose along the southwest border. Law enforcement personnel intercepted over eight thousand individuals attempting unauthorized entry in March, a documented rise from February's figures. Intelligence specialists monitoring the situation note that despite this statistical trend, order and security metrics have been maintained by current policy enforcement, reflecting ongoing control over border flow. However, legislative gridlock continues to delay essential resource provision for border control.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Ruler",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "result-0",
          "result-1"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.78
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "A surge challenging containment capacity occurred in March as seasonal conditions increased border pressure. Those subject to processing by federal law enforcement agents numbered 8,268, representing a documented rise in border encounters. Despite this, the current outcome reflecting border policy shows crossings remain near multi-decade lows. This structural control is threatened by a failure to provide essential resources for state security, as government officials remain deadlocked over funding in a pending reconciliation package.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Ruler",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "result-0",
          "result-1"
        ],
