    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "The spring weather, a recurring environmental factor, contributed to increased border activity. Border enforcement agents restoring order apprehended 8,268 people along the southwest border, an increase from the prior month. While this demonstrates enforcement actions rising in response to pressure, year-to-date immigration statistics remain low. This security force effectiveness is undermined by legislators failing to secure enforcement funding, creating a political deadlock that risks the stability of border security policy.",
